Title: The Mirror and the Font
Order: 17
Production Code: 1x17

INT. TELASSAR - AI'S SECRET CHAMBER - NIGHT

AMB: dripping water, an underground stillness

Restless since his betrothal, [[Reuel Briggs]] asks [[Ai]] to show him what's become of the world he left. Ai uncovers a polished disk — for the past — and a stone font of water — for the present.

AI
Think of a face. I will reflect it.

Reuel thinks of the river. The disk shows him the canoe, [[Aubrey Livingston]], [[Molly Vance]], and [[Dianthe Lusk]], gliding over the water — then nothing, when he asks it to show Dianthe's face as she last appeared on earth.

AI (CONT'D)
The disk cannot err. If it shows nothing of her death, then your friend still lives.

They try the font instead — and Dianthe's face, worn with grief, looks back at them from the water.

REUEL BRIGGS
Her very self. Alive.

They check Molly's fate on the disk: her face, on a riverbed among the reeds. Confirmed dead. Then, at Reuel's request, the font shows him his enemy — Aubrey's face, then, close behind it, Jim Titus's.

AI
Two. I thought so.

A final, harder vision: the Livingston parlor, Aubrey's arm around Dianthe's waist. Reuel goes ashen and collapses.

INT. TELASSAR - REUEL'S CHAMBER - NIGHT (LATER)

AMB: silence

He wakes to a pressure on his brow, a presence beside him he can't see.

DIANTHE LUSK (V.O.)
Reuel. It is I. I am not dead, my husband — but I am lost to you. The friend you gave me to has taken the power over me that should have only ever been yours.

REUEL BRIGGS
(to the empty room)
Fool. Dupe. To leave you in the hands of that monster and go chasing gold instead.

He resolves, then and there, to get home and confront Aubrey — if Telassar will let him leave at all.
